{
  "duration": 271.41600000000847,
  "chapters": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 133.15200000000414
    },
    {
      "start": 133.15200000000414,
      "end": 271.41600000000847
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1,
      "text": "Welcome back.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 1.5199999809265137,
      "end": 6.294359048207601,
      "text": "A banked turn is a lovely example of one diagram doing more work than a pile",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 6.294359048207601,
      "end": 6.420000076293945,
      "text": "of",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 6.420000076293945,
      "end": 6.880000114440918,
      "text": "memorized equations.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 7.340000152587891,
      "end": 9.34000015258789,
      "text": "We already found the frictionless speed.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 9.899999618530273,
      "end": 12.779999732971191,
      "text": "Now let's find the allowed range when static friction is available.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 13.5,
      "end": 16.700000762939453,
      "text": "This is an ideal particle model, not driving advice.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 17.739999771118164,
      "end": 20.18000030517578,
      "text": "The road rises toward the outside.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 21.200000762939453,
      "end": 23.579999923706055,
      "text": "Choose horizontal inward and vertical upward axes.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 24.059999465942383,
      "end": 26.540000915527344,
      "text": "The normal reaction points upward and inward.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 27.520000457763672,
      "end": 31.959999084472656,
      "text": "At a speed above the frictionless value, the car tends to slip outward and up",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 31.959999084472656,
      "end": 35.84000015258789,
      "text": "the bank, so friction acts down the bank: inward and downward.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 36.65999984741211,
      "end": 40.02000045776367,
      "text": "At the upper limiting speed its magnitude is mu times N.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 40.7599983215332,
      "end": 46.18000030517578,
      "text": "The inward equation is N sine theta plus mu N cosine theta equals m v squared",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 46.18000030517578,
      "end": 46.779998779296875,
      "text": "over r.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 47.58000183105469,
      "end": 53.209999084472656,
      "text": "The vertical equation is N cosine theta minus mu N sine theta equals m",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 53.209999084472656,
      "end": 54.31999969482422,
      "text": "g.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 54.31999969482422,
      "end": 57.119998931884766,
      "text": "Notice that N is not m g.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 57.119998931884766,
      "end": 58.68000030517578,
      "text": "Divide the first equation by the second.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 59.400001525878906,
      "end": 63.79999923706055,
      "text": "After dividing numerator and denominator by cosine theta, v squared over r g",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 63.79999923706055,
      "end": 68.27999877929688,
      "text": "becomes tangent theta plus mu, divided by one minus mu tangent theta.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 69.37999725341797,
      "end": 73.27999877929688,
      "text": "Let's use tangent theta equal to three quarters, mu equal to one quarter,",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 73.73999786376953,
      "end": 76.44000244140625,
      "text": "radius twenty five meters, and g equal to ten.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 77.08000183105469,
      "end": 81.5,
      "text": "The ratio is one divided by thirteen sixteenths, or sixteen thirteenths.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 82.33999633789062,
      "end": 86.9800033569336,
      "text": "Therefore maximum speed squared is four thousand over thirteen, and maximum",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 86.9800033569336,
      "end": 90.23999786376953,
      "text": "speed is approximately seventeen point five four meters per second.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 91.4800033569336,
      "end": 92.94000244140625,
      "text": "Pause before calling that answer valid.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 93.69999694824219,
      "end": 97.69999694824219,
      "text": "The denominator is positive, so the vertical balance permits a positive normal",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 97.69999694824219,
      "end": 99.04000091552734,
      "text": "force at this limiting state.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 99.76000213623047,
      "end": 103.81999969482422,
      "text": "If the denominator were zero or negative, do not take a square root of an",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 103.81999969482422,
      "end": 106.41999816894531,
      "text": "invalid expression and call it a real speed boundary.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 107.44000244140625,
      "end": 110.41999816894531,
      "text": "Return to the friction inequality and contact assumptions.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 111.08000183105469,
      "end": 114.73999786376953,
      "text": "Our formula is a model with a domain, not a universal rule.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 115.5199966430664,
      "end": 119.4000015258789,
      "text": "For this numerical case, the normal reaction divided by m g at the upper",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 119.4000015258789,
      "end": 122.91999816894531,
      "text": "boundary is twenty over thirteen.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 122.91999816894531,
      "end": 126.87076627291165,
      "text": "Friction has a downward component, so the normal's upward component must",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 126.87076627291165,
      "end": 127.19999694824219,
      "text": "supply",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 127.19999694824219,
      "end": 127.94000244140625,
      "text": "more than the weight.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 128.9199981689453,
      "end": 133.0399932861328,
      "text": "That check helps explain why simply setting N equal to m g would fail.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 133.15200000000414,
      "end": 134.65200000000414,
      "text": "Now reduce the speed.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 135.39200000954088,
      "end": 139.07200007629808,
      "text": "Below the frictionless value, the car tends to slip inward and down the bank.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 140.03200011444505,
      "end": 144.01199965668138,
      "text": "Static friction reverses: it points up the bank, outward and upward.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 144.75200038147386,
      "end": 149.8520007629436,
      "text": "At a positive lower limiting speed, the inward equation is N sine theta minus",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 149.8520007629436,
      "end": 153.3520007629436,
      "text": "mu N cosine theta equals m v squared over r.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 153.95199923706468,
      "end": 159.65200000000414,
      "text": "The vertical equation is N cosine theta plus mu N sine theta equals m g.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 159.65200000000414,
      "end": 160.5120006103557,
      "text": "Divide them carefully.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 161.19200091553148,
      "end": 165.95199923706468,
      "text": "The lower speed squared is r g times tangent theta minus mu, divided by one",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 165.95199923706468,
      "end": 167.09199862671312,
      "text": "plus mu tangent theta.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 167.97199969482836,
      "end": 172.91430680025954,
      "text": "Use our same twenty five meter radius, g ten, tangent theta three quarters,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 172.91430680025954,
      "end": 173.1119990844768,
      "text": "and",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 173.1119990844768,
      "end": 173.71200137329515,
      "text": "mu one quarter.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 174.39200167847093,
      "end": 178.81199984741625,
      "text": "The ratio is one half divided by nineteen sixteenths, or eight nineteenths.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 179.45199923706468,
      "end": 183.69200091553148,
      "text": "Minimum speed squared is two thousand over nineteen, so minimum speed is about",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 183.69200091553148,
      "end": 185.47199969482836,
      "text": "ten point two six meters per second.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 186.03200106811937,
      "end": 189.39200167847093,
      "text": "The frictionless speed is the square root of one hundred eighty seven point",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 189.39200167847093,
      "end": 192.431998779301,
      "text": "five, about thirteen point six nine.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 192.431998779301,
      "end": 195.19200091553148,
      "text": "It lies between the two limits, exactly as we hoped.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 195.89200167847093,
      "end": 200.35456384825508,
      "text": "At that middle speed, friction can be zero; static friction is not always mu",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 200.35456384825508,
      "end": 200.47199969482836,
      "text": "N.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 201.13200335693773,
      "end": 202.75199847412523,
      "text": "What if the coefficient were one instead?",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 203.13200335693773,
      "end": 206.2119975585979,
      "text": "The expression for the lower squared speed becomes negative.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 206.67199664307054,
      "end": 208.97199969482836,
      "text": "That does not create an imaginary physical speed.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 209.5120006103557,
      "end": 213.5319972534221,
      "text": "At rest, force balance on the slope requires friction divided by normal",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 213.5319972534221,
      "end": 215.45200305176195,
      "text": "reaction equal to tangent theta.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 216.07199816894945,
      "end": 220.07558907064217,
      "text": "Our tangent is three quarters, less than the available coefficient one, so",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 220.07558907064217,
      "end": 220.29199938965257,
      "text": "rest",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 220.29199938965257,
      "end": 222.97199969482836,
      "text": "is possible and the physical lower speed is zero.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 223.6119990844768,
      "end": 227.7466174034747,
      "text": "For the general check, solve for the signed required friction f directed up",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 227.7466174034747,
      "end": 227.9120021362346,
      "text": "the",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 227.9120021362346,
      "end": 228.1119990844768,
      "text": "bank.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 228.7119975585979,
      "end": 233.45200305176195,
      "text": "Its ratio to N is tangent theta minus q, divided by one plus q tangent theta,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 233.89199786377367,
      "end": 236.431998779301,
      "text": "where q is v squared over r g.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 236.431998779301,
      "end": 239.27200274658617,
      "text": "Demand the absolute value of that ratio be no greater than mu.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 239.73200183105882,
      "end": 242.29199938965257,
      "text": "That single inequality checks either friction direction.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 242.85199694824632,
      "end": 246.23994823671413,
      "text": "For example, at ten meters per second in our original quarter coefficient",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 246.23994823671413,
      "end": 246.47199969482836,
      "text": "case,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 247.0120006103557,
      "end": 248.0920024414104,
      "text": "q is zero point four.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 248.77200274658617,
      "end": 253.0920024414104,
      "text": "Required friction divided by N is about zero point two six nine, above one",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 253.0920024414104,
      "end": 255.0120006103557,
      "text": "quarter, so that speed is not allowed.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 255.63200335693773,
      "end": 260.49199633789476,
      "text": "At fourteen meters per second it is about minus zero point zero two one four,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 260.49199633789476,
      "end": 261.3120036621135,
      "text": "safely within the bound.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 261.6120067138713,
      "end": 264.2320018310588,
      "text": "The negative sign means friction acts down the bank.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 265.0120006103557,
      "end": 268.9248216709276,
      "text": "State the model, resolve actual forces, and test the inequality before",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 268.9248216709276,
      "end": 269.37200122070726,
      "text": "trusting",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 269.37200122070726,
      "end": 271.0120006103557,
      "text": "a memorized maximum or minimum.",
      "chapter": 1
    }
  ]
}
